WHY MTIME ALONE IS NOT A VERDICT
  The fifteen worst apimarket report faces all carry the SAME html mtime
  (2026-11-25 09:58) while their json halves date from 2026-10-25, and
  git status is clean. A bulk rewrite or restore of identical bytes leaves
  exactly that trace. So the census classifies on committed history instead:
  a split is claimed only when the two halves' last commits differ.

